From f6a533ead3411d2162af27fd4072ea3d2b12c602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:33:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(input): retain and transport native player permissions

Bedrock 1.26.51 protocol 2193 sends packet 196 as a single unsigned varint permission mask. Target BDS captures establish all eleven categories and the absence of a position field. Movement disables its child categories even when their individual bits are clear.

Retain each replacement per connection, filter held auth input immediately, and transport versioned snapshots after joining and late channel registration. Preserve unknown bits. Java local prediction and camera input require client integration; manual mount interactions remain incomplete.

Keep raw movement and jump/sneak edges independent of the permission-filtered controls. Negotiate a separate client sample channel so direct and ViaProxy clients can preserve physical input before local filtering. Ordinary Java clients retain raw samples from their standard input packets. Latch button edges between auth ticks and keep shield use out of raw sneak input.

Native 1.26.51 Script API comparisons establish normalized keyboard diagonals, positive left and negative right raw X, and movement/jump/sneak input while movement is locked. Live BDS tests validate locked position with raw input through ViaProxy.
